- When `treefiles = true`, nbd-server stores data in files of the form `exportname/TREEXXXX/.../FILEXXXX`. TREEXXXX and FILEXXXX are auto-generated directory names and path names for individual block files.
- Files and directories are automatically created. When the corresponding block is marked as unused, the file is deleted.
- The size of an individual block file is fixed at 4096 bytes (TREEPAGESIZE).
- One folder contains at most 1024 files/subdirectories (TREEDIRSIZE).
- An appropriate nesting depth is created in order to build a filesystem totaling filesize bytes.
- Mutually exclusive with multifile (-m); treefiles takes precedence.
- filesize must be specified.

